@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+The seasonal menu uses autonomous `<coffee-card>` custom elements, registered by
+the `coffee-card.js` ES module. Each card owns an open shadow root with its markup
+and styles. Existing page theme variables (`--primary`, `--text`, and `--accent`)
+are inherited, with standalone fallbacks. The `card`, `name`, and `link` shadow
+parts allow additional styling.
+
+```html
+<coffee-card
+  name="Maple Oat Latte"
+  description="Creamy oat milk with maple syrup."
+  href="/menu/seasonal"
+  price="5.50"
+  featured>
+</coffee-card>
+```
+
+Attributes and identically named JavaScript properties reflect in both directions:
+
+| Attribute/property | Type | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `name`, `description`, `href` | String | Default to `''`; assigning `null` or `undefined` removes the attribute. |
+| `price` | Number | Defaults to `0`; only displayed when the attribute is present. Invalid, negative, or non-finite values read as `0`. Assignments serialize a nonnegative finite number (or `0`); `null`/`undefined` removes the attribute. Displayed in USD. |
+| `featured` | Boolean | Presence means true, including `featured="false"`. Assign `false` or remove the attribute to turn it off. Displays a seasonal favorite label. |
+
+```js
+const card = document.querySelector('coffee-card');
+card.name = 'Maple Oat Latte';
+card.price = 5.5;                // Reflects price="5.5"
+card.featured = true;            // Adds featured=""
+card.setAttribute('price', '6'); // card.price is now 6
+card.featured = false;           // Removes featured
+```
+
+Cards render their current attributes on connection and react to subsequent
+attribute changes. Properties assigned before registration are recovered on
+upgrade. Disconnecting removes the card's click listener; reconnecting restores
+it without duplicating listeners or rebuilding the shadow tree.
+
+Activating a details link emits a bubbling, composed `coffee-select` event with
+`{ name, href, price, featured }` in `event.detail`, while preserving native link
+navigation. Only HTTP(S) destinations (including relative URLs) are enabled.
